{"availability":"available","full":"utosrad/whop-tasks-mvp","name":"whop-tasks-mvp","description":"AI-verified task marketplace. Creators post paid tasks with proof requirements, OpenAI grades worker proof under a strict JSON schema, and approval writes payout, fee and budget rows to a demo ledger. Next.js 16, Prisma, Postgres.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-23T19:46:54Z","updated":"2026-08-06T23:45:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://whop-tasks-mvp.vercel.app","topics":["llm","marketplace","nextjs","openai","postgresql","prisma","structured-outputs","tailwindcss","typescript","zod"],"demo":"https://whop-tasks-mvp.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.483Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.483Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.483Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.483Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A task marketplace where a creator's payout only clears after a model reads the worker's proof against the requirements the creator wrote.","Creators post paid tasks with explicit proof requirements. Workers submit a URL, a screenshot, and text. The server sends that proof to OpenAI under a strict JSON schema and stores the structured verdict. The creator approves, rejects, or asks for more proof using that verdict as evidence. Approving writes three rows to a demo ledger: worker payout, platform fee, creator budget debit.","Built in one day for a Whop interview. It is a working demo, not a payments product. Nothing here moves real money."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/utosrad/whop-tasks-mvp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"13d417fe1cd0dd5c0f107d18b23500a5de8ff22c1ba23c08b4b62a514525e344","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.701Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:22.701Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A task marketpla